 {"q": "In Leviticus 19, what does the command 'You shall be holy' turn out to mean?", "options": ["Living apart from other people", "Mainly ritual purity", "Everyday justice and kindness: leaving food for the poor, paying wages promptly, protecting the deaf and blind, loving the neighbour", "Becoming a priest"], "answer": 2, "why": "Holiness is shown in ordinary life."},
