 {"q": "How did Thomas Aquinas explain why Christians keep some laws of Moses and not others?", "options": ["They keep only those Jesus repeated", "He divided the law into moral precepts, which bind all forever, ceremonial precepts, fulfilled in Christ, and judicial precepts, for Israel as a nation", "He said all the law was abolished", "He said Christians must keep all 613"], "answer": 1, "why": "The threefold division, held in some form by most churches."},
